{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792402485,"nonce":"XBYGw3t34MJtsQ/ycFYJlxIrsoo=","title":"A file with a lowering error gets no names recorded, which likely leaves it without IDE answers","message":"In `compile_file_with_shared_state_ex_with_parsed` (compiler/src/compilation/driver.rs), `let typed_file = lowered.map_err(...)?` returns before `record_definition_locations` and `collect_references` run. So the file being edited gets no position index while it has any type error, and the LSP's FileSymbolIndex for it comes back empty.\n\nI have not tested this end to end. If it holds, hover, definition, references, highlights, outline and semantic tokens all disappear while the user is fixing the error, which is when they are wanted most.\n\nNeeded: lowering that keeps the declarations and statements it managed to type (error recovery per member or statement), and recording names from that partial file. Until then, the LSP could keep the previous good index for the file.","files":null}]}